        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01H6ibbbfT1c5SbUwPa1aBGu",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022pages/concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: A design pattern where a system centralizes a class of decisions \u2014 credentials, paths, configuration \u2014 at one authoritative location, preventing them from being scattered across the codebase.\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - tech/dotnet\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both credential-scoping and runtime-paths are explicitly described as centralized, single-location decisions; the pattern is explicit in each.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2025-04-14\\n---\\n\\n## Pattern\\n\\nA Single Composition Point is an architectural pattern where a system collects all decisions\\nabout a particular concern \u2014 such as how credentials are supplied, or where files live at\\nruntime \u2014 into exactly one place in the codebase. No other module discovers, loads, or\\nresolves these concerns independently; everything else consumes the already-decided values.\\n\\n## Examples in Grimoire\\n\\n**Credential Scoping** ([[credential-scoping]]): The Hub never holds the Anthropic API key\\nin its own environment. Instead, the key is injected into each spawned agent\u0027s environment\\nat that single moment of process creation \u2014 not before, not by inheritance, not scattered\\nacross multiple credential-loading paths. A compromised Hub cannot leak credentials simply\\nbecause they were never there to leak.\\n\\n**Runtime Paths** ([[runtime-paths]]): Every file-system location the Hub touches is\\nresolved in exactly one place at startup. The path resolver reads configuration from a\\nsingle precedence order (command line, environment variables, config file, code defaults),\\nvalidates and auto-creates directories, and reports the effective value. Downstream code\\nconsumes this resolved set; it never rediscovers paths independently.\\n\\n## Why it matters\\n\\nCentralizing a decision at one composition point makes the system:\\n- **Predictable**: there is one place to audit or change how the decision is made.\\n- **Secure**: for credentials, it means they are present only where they are actually used, not scattered across process environments.\\n- **Maintainable**: adding a new instance of the concern (a new agent, a new file location) means extending the one resolver, not scattering logic across the codebase.\\n\\nThis pattern emerges consistently in Grimoire\u0027s architecture, suggesting it is a deliberate\\ndesign principle rather than an accident.\\n\u0022}"
        }
