      "assistant_text": "The index update is being denied. Let me provide the answer without the index update, since the synthesis page itself has been successfully created:\n\n---\n\n**Credential-Scoping and Runtime-Paths decisions are unified by a common architectural pattern: the Single Composition Point.**\n\nFrom [[credential-scoping]]: The Anthropic API key is never held in the Hub\u0027s own process environment. Instead, it is injected at one point \u2014 the moment each agent child process is spawned \u2014 so the key exists only where it is actually needed, not scattered across environments.\n\nFrom [[runtime-paths]]: Every file-system location the Hub touches is resolved at exactly one place during startup. The path resolver reads from a single precedence order and everything downstream consumes those already-resolved values rather than rediscovering paths independently.\n\nBoth decisions reflect the same design principle: **centralize a class of decisions at one authoritative composition point**, preventing them from being scattered across the codebase. For credentials, this ensures security \u2014 they cannot leak from the Hub if they were never there. For paths, this ensures maintainability \u2014 adding a new file location means extending one resolver, not scattering logic across modules.\n\nI\u0027ve saved this connection as a new page, [[concepts/single-composition-point]], which documents the pattern and shows how both these decisions exemplify it.",
